- Welcome to Virgulas
  A local-first outliner for thinking in connected, expandable notes. This document is a guided tour: edit it freely, then choose storage when you are ready to keep your work.
- Start writing
  Click a node to edit its title. Press `Enter` to add the next node; when the current node has visible children, `Enter` adds the first child. Press `Escape` to leave editing.
  - Add detail with `Shift+Enter` to switch between a title and its optional description. Empty descriptions stay out of the way, and longer descriptions are previewed when you are browsing.
  - Use **bold**, __italic__, `code`, [links](https://virgulas.com), and images in a title or description. Markdown renders while browsing and returns to plain text while editing.
  - Type `#project` or `@name` in any note. Select the rendered pill to search for that tag or person.
  - Paste a line normally. Paste multiple lines, or text beginning with `-` or `+`, to turn a VMD outline fragment into nodes.
- Shape the outline
  Use `Tab` and `Shift+Tab` to indent or outdent the focused node. On mobile, swipe right or left instead. Use `Alt+↑` and `Alt+↓` to move a node among its siblings.
  - Select neighboring siblings with `Shift+↑` or `Shift+↓`, then move, indent, outdent, collapse, or delete the group together.
  - Press `Ctrl+Space`, or use the ▶/▼ control, to collapse and expand children.
  + A collapsed example
    - Child notes stay here until you expand this node.
    - Collapsing is useful for keeping a long plan calm and scannable.
  - Press `Ctrl+Backspace` to delete a node. Backspace on an empty title also deletes it; deleting a node with children asks for confirmation.
- Navigate and find
  Select any bullet to zoom into that node. Its children become your working view; use the breadcrumb to go back. On desktop, `Alt+→` zooms in and `Alt+←` zooms out.
  - Press `Escape` with no note focused to search on desktop; on mobile use the Search button in the status bar. Matching text is highlighted and non-matches are hidden.
  - Use `Tab` and `Shift+Tab` to move through results, then `Enter` or select a result to open it. Press `Escape` again to close search.
  - Press `Ctrl+C` with a title focused and no text selected to copy that node and its descendants as VMD.
- Turn notes into tasks
  Press `Ctrl+Enter` to cycle a focused note through plain, pending, and done. You can also begin its title with `[ ] ` or `[x] `.
  - [ ] Plan the next review due:2026-09-15
    Due dates appear as chips and overdue work is highlighted in the task list.
  - [ ] Pay rent due:2026-09-28 rec:1m
    Add `rec:1d`, `rec:1w`, `rec:1m`, or `rec:1y` beside a due date to repeat it. Completing a recurring task advances its date instead of marking it done.
  - Open Tasks with `Ctrl+Alt+K` or the checklist button in the status bar. It groups work into Pending, Scheduled, and Done for your current zoom; select a row to jump to it.
- Keep your work
  This tour is in memory only and disappears when the tab closes. Select **Enable Secure Storage** above to choose a persistent mode.
  - **Local** encrypts this browser's document with a passphrase you choose. The passphrase cannot be recovered.
  - **Remote** signs in with an account password, then encrypts and syncs your document with a separate passphrase. Other devices need both access to the account and the passphrase.
    Changes are synced after you pause typing. When edits conflict, choose which version of each field to keep.
  - **File** opens or creates a plain `.vmd` file on your device. Changes are saved back to the file after you pause typing.
  - In Local or Remote mode, Options lets you export or import a `.vmd` backup, change your encryption passphrase, and enable an optional biometric prompt on this device.
- Make it yours
  Select **Options** in the status bar to change theme, manage the current storage session, or open the source repository. The current mode and sync state are also shown there.
  - On desktop, `Ctrl+Alt+T` toggles theme, `Ctrl+Alt+W` toggles wide mode, and `Ctrl+Alt+D` opens developer diagnostics.
  - Select the **?** button for the complete keyboard shortcut reference.
